{"black_box_warning":{"current_value":"No FDA boxed warning identified in selected current DailyMed label.","fda_source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/008943s054lbl.pdf","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/008943s053%2C009388s039lbl.pdf","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/012945s048lbl.pdf"],"proposed_value":"No FDA boxed warning identified in selected current FDA labeling.","rationale":"The no-boxed-warning conclusion is supportable from FDA label PDFs that show ordinary WARNINGS sections but no BOXED WARNING section. The current value/source is not compliant because it cites DailyMed for the FDA boxed-warning field.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect"},"blocking_questions":[],"fact_checks":[{"current_value":"acetazolamide","field":"generic_name","proposed_value":"acetazolamide","rationale":"FDA labeling identifies acetazolamide/DIAMOX as the active drug.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/008943s054lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"acetazolamide sodium","field":"alternate_generic_names","proposed_value":"acetazolamide sodium","rationale":"FDA labeling for injection states each vial contains acetazolamide sodium equivalent to acetazolamide.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/008943s053%2C009388s039lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Yes","field":"available_in_us","proposed_value":"Yes","rationale":"FDA Orange Book/reference-standard listings and current FDA labeling show US acetazolamide products.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.fda.gov/media/103879/download?attachment=","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/008943s054lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Acetazolamide; Acetazolamide Sodium; Diamox","field":"trade_names","proposed_value":"Acetazolamide; Acetazolamide Sodium; Diamox; Diamox Sequels","rationale":"Current value omits DIAMOX SEQUELS, the FDA-labeled extended-release capsule brand. Existing generic product names are not contradicted, so retain and append the missing brand.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/012945s048lbl.pdf","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/008943s054lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Diamox; acetazolamide sodium","field":"pubmed_search_aliases","proposed_value":"Diamox; Diamox Sequels; acetazolamide sodium","rationale":"Add Diamox Sequels so the branded extended-release capsule alias is searchable.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/012945s048lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Oral tablet; extended-release capsule; IV injection as acetazolamide sodium","field":"formulations_available","proposed_value":"Oral tablet; extended-release capsule; IV injection as acetazolamide sodium","rationale":"FDA labels support tablets, extended-release capsules, and intravenous acetazolamide sodium injection.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/008943s054lbl.pdf","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/008943s053%2C009388s039lbl.pdf","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/012945s048lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Capsule; IV/IM injection; Long acting; Tablet","field":"filter_formulation","proposed_value":"Capsule; IV injection; Long acting; Tablet","rationale":"FDA labeling says the injection is for intravenous use and intramuscular administration is not recommended.","requires_user_approval":true,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/008943s053%2C009388s039lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Centrencephalic epilepsies; Absence; Generalized; Myoclonic; Adjunctive nonspecific epilepsy","field":"epilepsy_type","proposed_value":"Centrencephalic epilepsies; Absence; Generalized; Myoclonic; Adjunctive nonspecific epilepsy","rationale":"FDA labeling supports adjunctive use for centrencephalic epilepsies including petit mal/unlocalized seizures and describes results in petit mal, grand mal, mixed seizure patterns, and myoclonic jerk patterns.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/008943s053%2C009388s039lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Carbonic anhydrase inhibitor; FDA labeling states inhibition in the CNS appears to retard abnormal paroxysmal excessive neuronal discharge, while acknowledging that the basis of epilepsy benefit is not clearly known.","field":"mechanism_of_action","proposed_value":"Carbonic anhydrase inhibitor; FDA labeling states inhibition in the CNS appears to retard abnormal paroxysmal excessive neuronal discharge, while acknowledging that the basis of epilepsy benefit is not clearly known.","rationale":"FDA labeling supports the carbonic anhydrase mechanism and the uncertainty around epilepsy benefit.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/008943s053%2C009388s039lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Moderate","field":"mechanism_confidence","proposed_value":"Moderate","rationale":"Moderate confidence is reasonable because the mechanism is label-supported but the label states the basis of the epilepsy benefit is not clearly known.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/008943s053%2C009388s039lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"FDA/DailyMed labeling","field":"mechanism_source","proposed_value":"FDA Drugs@FDA/accessdata labeling","rationale":"Mechanism can be supported by FDA label PDFs; remove DailyMed from the named source.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/008943s053%2C009388s039lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"No broad enzyme induction/inhibition described in selected FDA label; label notes interactions including altered phenytoin metabolism and reduced primidone/metabolite concentrations through decreased absorption.","field":"enzyme_inducing_or_inhibiting","proposed_value":"No broad enzyme induction/inhibition described in selected FDA label; label notes interactions including altered phenytoin metabolism and reduced primidone/metabolite concentrations through decreased absorption.","rationale":"FDA labeling supports phenytoin and primidone interaction wording and does not describe broad CYP induction/inhibition.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/008943s053%2C009388s039lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"N/A 0%: FDA label lists paresthesia, hearing dysfunction/tinnitus, loss of appetite, taste alteration, GI disturbances, polyuria, drowsiness, confusion, rash, blood dyscrasias, electrolyte imbalance, and metabolic acidosis without quantified incidence percentages.","field":"adverse_symptoms_percentages","proposed_value":"N/A 0%: FDA label lists paresthesia, hearing dysfunction/tinnitus, loss of appetite, taste alteration, GI disturbances, polyuria, drowsiness, confusion, rash, blood dyscrasias, electrolyte imbalance, and metabolic acidosis without quantified incidence percentages.","rationale":"FDA adverse-reaction sections list these reactions qualitatively without incidence percentages.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/008943s053%2C009388s039lbl.pdf","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/012945s048lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"N/A - selected FDA/DailyMed label does not provide a half-life value.","field":"half_life_range","proposed_value":"6-14 hours; reported values vary by trusted NCBI sources, with StatPearls listing plasma half-life 6-9 hours and an NCBI Bookshelf epilepsy text listing elimination half-life 12-14 hours.","rationale":"The field should not remain N/A when trusted NCBI sources provide half-life values. The current statement is only true for the selected FDA label, not for the fact field overall.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK532282/","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK2597/"]},{"current_value":"N/A - selected FDA/DailyMed label does not identify a major metabolic organ; renal bicarbonate handling and urinary effects are clinically central.","field":"major_organ_for_metabolism","proposed_value":"No major metabolism; renal excretion is the primary route of elimination.","rationale":"NCBI sources state acetazolamide does not undergo metabolic alteration and is renally excreted.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK532282/","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK2597/"]},{"current_value":"1000 mg/day; FDA label notes doses above 1 g/day do not appear to improve results.","field":"maximum_approved_daily_dose","proposed_value":"1000 mg/day; FDA label notes doses above 1 g/day do not appear to improve results.","rationale":"FDA dosage labeling supports the 375-1000 mg/day optimum epilepsy range and notes doses above 1 g/day do not appear to improve results.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/008943s053%2C009388s039lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"375 mg/day or 8 mg/kg/day lower labeled epilepsy-adjunct range; individualized response noted in FDA label.","field":"minimum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"375 mg/day or 8 mg/kg/day lower labeled epilepsy-adjunct range; individualized response noted in FDA label.","rationale":"FDA labeling gives 8-30 mg/kg/day in divided doses, an optimum range of 375-1000 mg/day, and individualized response language.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/008943s053%2C009388s039lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Epilepsy adjunct: 8-30 mg/kg/day in divided doses; FDA label states optimum range appears to be 375-1000 mg/day.","field":"typical_doses_per_day","proposed_value":"Epilepsy adjunct: 8-30 mg/kg/day in divided doses; FDA label states optimum range appears to be 375-1000 mg/day.","rationale":"FDA epilepsy dosing section supports this text.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/008943s053%2C009388s039lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"No QT interval effect described in selected FDA label.","field":"qt_interval_effect","proposed_value":"No QT-related warning or effect identified in selected FDA labeling; absence of label language does not establish a proven no-effect finding.","rationale":"FDA labels reviewed do not describe QT effects, but label silence is not strong evidence for 'no known meaningful QT effect'.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"insufficient_evidence","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/008943s054lbl.pdf","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/008943s053%2C009388s039lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"No known meaningful QT effect","field":"filter_qt_effect","proposed_value":"No QT-related warning/effect identified in selected FDA labeling","rationale":"The stronger 'no known meaningful QT effect' claim is not directly established by the cited FDA label; a label-limited statement is supportable.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"insufficient_evidence","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/008943s054lbl.pdf","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/008943s053%2C009388s039lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Approved Prior to Jan 1, 1982 (FDA Orange Book)","field":"year_fda_cleared","proposed_value":"Approved Prior to Jan 1, 1982 (FDA Orange Book)","rationale":"FDA Orange Book data-file documentation defines this approval-date phrase, and acetazolamide/DIAMOX appears in FDA Orange Book/labeling sources. The deterministic openFDA-label concordance warning is a source mismatch, not a contradiction of the Orange Book date.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.fda.gov/drugs/drug-approvals-and-databases/orange-book-data-files","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/appletter/2025/008943Orig1s054ltr.pdf"]},{"current_value":"FDA Orange Book products file; FDA/DailyMed labeling","field":"evidence_sources","proposed_value":"FDA Orange Book data files; FDA Drugs@FDA/accessdata labeling; NCBI Bookshelf; PubMed","rationale":"DailyMed should be removed from the named row sources, and NCBI/PubMed should be added for half-life/metabolism and RCT-gap support.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.fda.gov/drugs/drug-approvals-and-databases/orange-book-data-files","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/008943s054lbl.pdf","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK532282/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6797857/"]},{"current_value":"N/A","field":"pubmed_phase_ii_iii_rct_links","proposed_value":"N/A","rationale":"No existing PubMed RCT links were supplied, and no qualifying acetazolamide phase II/III placebo-controlled epilepsy RCT was identified. The notable PubMed acetazolamide epilepsy paper PMID 6797857 has no abstract and is identified by the NICE/NCBI evidence review as incorrect study design for the relevant evidence review.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6797857/","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK581157/"]},{"current_value":"No qualifying phase II/III placebo-controlled randomized epilepsy RCT was retained in the PubMed RCT audit/gap review as of 05-19-2026; RCT section set to N/A per current scope.","field":"rct_pubmed_verification_notes","proposed_value":"No qualifying phase II/III placebo-controlled randomized epilepsy RCT was found/retained in the PubMed RCT audit/gap review as of 05-20-2026; RCT section remains N/A.","rationale":"Update the audit date to the current audit date while retaining the same conclusion.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6797857/","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK581157/"]},{"current_value":"No FDA boxed warning identified in selected current DailyMed label.","field":"fda_black_box_warning","proposed_value":"No FDA boxed warning identified in selected current FDA labeling.","rationale":"Conclusion is supported by FDA label PDFs, but the current wording relies on DailyMed, which is not permissible for this field.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/008943s054lbl.pdf","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/008943s053%2C009388s039lbl.pdf","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/012945s048lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"FDA/DailyMed SPL; status=no_boxed_warning_in_selected_label; setid=58093032-8480-4d0f-82be-92e643bdbea4; published=Jan 16, 2026; title=ACETAZOLAMIDE (ACETAZOLAMIDE SODIUM) INJECTION, POWDER, FOR SOLUTION [SAGENT PHARMACEUTICALS]; url=https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=58093032-8480-4d0f-82be-92e643bdbea4","field":"fda_black_box_warning_source","proposed_value":"FDA Drugs@FDA/accessdata labels; status=no_boxed_warning_identified_in_selected_fda_labels; checked labels: DIAMOX tablets NDA 0